   "date": "2017-03-30",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Human Rights Legislation Amendment Bill was introduced to reform the Australian Human Rights Commission’s complaints handling processes, implementing unanimous recommendations from the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Human Rights' 2017 report on freedom of speech, and aiming to prevent unmeritorious complaints like those involving QUT students and cartoonist Bill Leak."
